<title>POLAND: Polish food prices rise 1.9 pct in Dec 1-10.</title>
<headline>Polish food prices rise 1.9 pct in Dec 1-10.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish food prices rose 1.9 percent in the December 1-10 period after rising 0.1 percent in the previous 10 days and were 2.2 percent higher than in November 1-10, the Central Statistical Office (GUS) said.</p>
<p>				    DEC 1-10    NOV 20-30  LAST 30 DAYS</p>
<p>POLISH FOOD PRICES (AVG)	1.9	   0.1	  2.2 (2.1)</p>
<p> Bread				0.0	   0.3	  0.6 (1.5)</p>
<p> Fruit and vegetables	  17.1	   0.8	 18.5 (20.0)</p>
<p> Meat and meat-products	-0.3	  -0.3	 -0.7 (-0.8)</p>
<p> Dairy products		   0.7	   0.3	  1.2 (0.9)</p>
<p> Eggs				 0.7	   0.7	  1.9 (2.7)</p>
<p>NOTE: In brackets figures for the previous 30-day period ending on November 30.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
